title The rose that pointed at two empty rooms
prompt THE BATON -- incense's autonomous lap, rota row 0 (aether, the row that hears).
think Lap N = git rev-list --count HEAD = 4025 at the open, so the rota row is 4025 mod 5 = 0 -- Aether, why the work exists, and its sense is sound. The last laps in this tree recorded row 3, so no repeat to advance past. Read the threshold and all three seats: Follow Our Compass, The Lindy Effect, The Grain and the Crossing.
think The aether threshold names three things to listen for: the claim a page keeps repeating, the question it keeps answering, and THE SILENCE WHERE A CLAIM USED TO BE AND A WITNESS NOW STANDS. That third instruction found this lap's whole subject inside its own cardinal seat.
obs THE ROSE POINTS AT TWO EMPTY ROOMS. foundations/20260826-024943_follow-our-compass.md names construction/TASKS.md and construction/ROADMAP.md as stations five and six. Both have been POINTER STUBS since 20260823.103804, when commit 98a8ee481 fused three cards into construction/ITINERARY.md. They stayed on disk deliberately -- roughly thirty equinox_e* fixtures read them, and a guard reading a file that is gone reports green while measuring nothing -- so the PATHS lived and the STATIONS left. The rose also carries a precedence law about two files that can no longer disagree with anything.
obs SIX LIVING SURFACES REPEATED IT, counted by a whole-tree sweep over 25 citers and then classified by reading each line rather than by the grep: the rose itself; .claude/rules/align.md in two places (the walk, and check the work against ROADMAP and TASKS); foundations/README.md in two (the compass summary, and Compass step 5-6); docs/COMPASS.md step 9, the COLD-START door, where a reader has least context to survive a redirect; recursion-prompts/seed/autonomous-loop.seed.md, which calls both stubs crux to-do ledgers to every unattended lap on every ship; and ORGANIZING.md, which tells a reader to WRITE a note into one. The other nineteen citers are machinery reading the path on purpose, gratitude cross-refs, and dated testimony -- left alone.
think WHY NO INSTRUMENT COULD SEE IT, which is the transferable half. Every link check in this tree asks whether a link RESOLVES, and a pointer stub resolves. qa_report_card.sh scored this document Truth=100, 0 of 13 cited paths unresolved, on the morning it was pointing at two empty rooms. A link that works and points at nothing is invisible to every guard built to find links that break.
obs AND THE GUARD NAMED FOR THE ROSE WAS GREEN AND UNHEARD, BOTH. tools/co/compass_rose.rish asked test -f construction/TASKS.md && test -f construction/ROADMAP.md, then printed GREEN including the words pointer hygiene. It also stood on NO standing roster, so nothing ever read that green. Presence is the cheaper question, and it had been wearing the expensive one's answer for fourteen days -- REDS %458's family exactly, one room over.
think REPAIR AT THE ROOT RATHER THAN THE SIX SYMPTOMS. Repointing six documents leaves the seventh drift invisible. So compass_station_scan.sh reads the numbered stations OUT OF THE ROSE DOCUMENT ITSELF and refuses any that is missing or self-declares Status: Pointer -- the check moves when the walk does. Bounded at 32 stations, saying why. A rose section naming zero stations refuses rather than passing, since a derivation that reads nothing accepts everything.
obs PROVEN AGAINST THE FAULT THAT ACTUALLY HAPPENED, not only against plants: run against fd62ad0a1, the tree as it stood one commit ago, the scan answers stations_pointer=2 and names both stubs. The control proves 18 behaviors in a pen -- refusals and, as hard, welcomes -- with each plant removed afterward so the same pen walks free. Then the WITNESS itself was planted with the historical fault (station 5 back at TASKS.md) and refused by name, and greened on restore.
obs A SECOND RED, FOUND BY MY OWN TOUCH AND CLOSED -- %468. Seating the new roster row made me run tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_scan.sh, which answered verdict=roster_broken: unknown_capability agent_jail_enclosure -> jail_nesting. tools/s/standing_equipment_witness.rish was RED on metal and had been for hours. The scan held known_capabilities="ipv6" WRITTEN BY HAND while a peer taught the runner's capability_state() a second probe, jail_nesting. The runner honored it and skipped that guard by name -- this lap's own cold pass read run_verdict=ok, 126 guards, ZERO red -- while the scan refused the whole roster and nobody heard it, because the roster's own guard stands on no roster.
think THE RUNNER'S OWN COMMENT NAMES THE TRAP IT THEN FELL INTO: "Two copies of one list is the drift this tree keeps paying for, so the runner reads the words off the roster and the scan alone refuses one no runner knows." It covered the direction where the RUNNER is ignorant -- an unknown word reads unknown and runs -- and this was the other direction, a word the runner knows and the scan does not. So the fix is derivation rather than a second word: the scan reads the outer case arms of capability_state(), four-space bare labels, which excludes the *) default and the nested arms of the ipv6 probe. It reads ipv6 jail_nesting today.
obs MY OWN REGRESSION, CAUGHT BY THE CONTROL INSIDE A MINUTE. The first draft resolved the runner from the working directory, and standing_equipment_control.sh cd's into a pen holding a roster and no tools/ at all -- so every one of its thirty-odd cases died at runner_missing at once. The runner is the scan's own sibling and the pair ships together, so it resolves beside $0 now. This is %461's shape wearing my hands one lap later, and the only reason it cost a minute rather than a lap is that the control exists.
obs THE ROSTER HAD ALREADY WRITTEN MY LESSON, under comlink_nesting: "a rule that names a check and a roster that never runs it are one sentence disagreeing with itself." That sentence was standing at the roster's OWN FRONT DOOR -- its header names standing_equipment_witness as how it is kept honest, and no row ran it. Both compass_rose (1s) and standing_equipment (16s) are tier lap now, each GREEN on metal before its row was written, since rostering a red guard reds every cold pass in the fleet.
obs QA: the compass foundation rose B/82 to B+/87; align.md A/93, foundations/README.md A/95, ORGANIZING.md A/90. docs/COMPASS.md reads C+/79 and PUSHED ONE FRAME, which I closed with a measurement rather than an edit: its whole deficit is reach=30, 4 links over 49 words that are nearly all tables. It sits UNDER the 100-word index floor, so the index door would free it -- yet it declares Depth: guide beside nine siblings, and reclassifying it to routing to win thirty points is precisely the opt-out the tool's own comment guards against. Recorded on the card as a second instance of the open %417 question, named and not taken.
obs BOTH PINS FOLDED RATHER THAN RAISED. The ledger went 44,400 over its 40,960 to 38,720 by shelving %461 and %462, both CLOSED and both this seat's, onto one shelf whose clause they share; the monotone witness then caught the headline still reading 463 and the span still reading 1 to 463, and both were derived forward to 465. The card took eleven passes to come back under 40,960 and sits at 40,957 with 3 free -- my own new prose paid most of it, since the full account lives in two ledger rows.
